{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nclaim={\\\"id\\\":\\\"C7-accept-reply-higher-ballot-is-a-rejection\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"concern\\\":\\\"bounded_liveness\\\",\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"When a replica leading the accept phase for an instance receives an AcceptReply whose ballot is higher than the ballot of that round, the reply must be treated as a rejection: the leader must count it as a nack and, once a majority has nacked, make a new ballot and run prepare again, instead of leaving the round unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\",\\\"S5-broadcasters\\\",\\\"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"One leader in the ACCEPTED state for instance (1,0) at ballot 3 receives one AcceptReply with ballot 5 from a peer that has promised a higher ballot; N=3 with Thrifty and IsLeader true.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"the reply is the one a peer sends when its stored bal exceeds the accept round's ballot\\\",\\\"the leader's round is otherwise unchanged\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"message loss and the timeout-driven recovery path, which can also advance a stalled instance\\\",\\\"the pre-accept side, whose replies cannot carry a different ballot at all\\\",\\\"the safety of ignoring such a reply (ignoring it is conservative, not unsafe)\\\"]},\n \\\"pending\\\":[],\n \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB8-accept-reply\\\"],\n  \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"handleAcceptReply has a branch for a reply whose ballot exceeds the round (increment nacks and, past a majority, make a ballot and prepare), but the handler returns earlier when the reply's ballot differs from lastTriedBallot, so that branch cannot run; this check observes the branch's own duty against the value the run produces.\\\",\n  \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Applies whenever a peer answers an accept round with a higher ballot, which handleAccept does after printing a smaller-ballot message and replying with its stored bal.\\\",\n  \\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"whether progress in that situation is fully covered by the 10s recovery timeout, which this check does not exercise\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}}\nb8={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB8-accept-reply\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1008,\\\"end_line\\\":1064,\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Accept-reply handling: the ballot-equality gate, the nack branch behind it, and the accept-quorum commit.\\\",\n \\\"associations\\\":[{\\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C7-accept-reply-higher-ballot-is-a-rejection\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The gate that returns on any ballot mismatch precedes the branch that would count the rejection, which is what the check exercises.\\\"}],\n \\\"pending\\\":[]}\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: a leader in ACCEPTED state at ballot 3 receives an AcceptReply with ballot 5 from a peer that has promised a higher ballot. Prefix: the harness builds the leader's round with the reviewed constructors and calls the real handleAcceptReply. Controls: the events print the round's ballot and status, then the reply ballot together with the nack count, accept count, whether any message was emitted and the status after the call.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":claim[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB8-accept-reply\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that prepares an ACCEPTED leader round and delivers one higher-ballot AcceptReply to the real handler, reporting the counters and any emitted message.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: the Replica is constructed in-package with buffer peer writers, the round is built with the package's own instance and bookkeeping constructors, and the reply is delivered directly to the handler\\\",\\\"the reply is the value handleAccept produces for a peer with a higher stored bal; no protocol code is modified\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"accept_round\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"leader_round\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"last_tried_ballot\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB8-accept-reply\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"Both sides are the implementation's own: the round is the state a leader reaches after the accept branch, and the reply is what handleAccept sends when its bal exceeds the accept ballot.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"N=3, Thrifty, IsLeader true, one reply.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the timeout-driven recovery path is not exercised\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-accept-reply\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-accept-reply\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"accept_reply_higher_ballot\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB8-accept-reply\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB8-accept-reply\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports the rejection counters and whether the leader reacted, which is the branch's own duty.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The leader was in the accept phase and the reply's ballot exceeded the round's.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"accept_round.instance\\\"}],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"accept_round\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-accept-reply\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"accept_reply_higher_ballot\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"nacks\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"instance\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A reply whose ballot exceeds the accept round's ballot must be recorded as one nack.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the check does not exercise the timeout-driven recovery that can also advance the instance\\\",\\\"the majority-nack consequence is not reached because the check delivers a single reply\\\"]}\nq={\\\"audit_spec_version\\\":9,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"ready_for_check\\\",\\\"preferred_check\\\":\\\"direct_test\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"When a peer answers an accept round with an AcceptReply whose ballot is higher than the round's ballot, does the leader count that reply as a rejection (and, past a majority, make a new ballot and prepare again), or does the ballot-equality gate return first so the rejection is never recorded?\\\",\n \\\"importance\\\":\\\"A leader whose accept round is rejected by peers with higher ballots never learns it: the round stays in ACCEPTED with no nacks and no new prepare, so progress depends on the 10s execution timeout instead of the handler's own rejection path. That is a liveness cost on the collision path rather than a safety problem, since ignoring the reply is conservative.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S12-handleAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S11-handleAccept\\\",\\\"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\\\",\\\"S5-broadcasters\\\",\\\"S21-quorum-sizes\\\",\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"S4-execute-loop\\\"],\n \\\"contexts\\\":[\\\"leader in ACCEPTED state at ballot 3\\\",\\\"peer that has promised ballot 5 answers the accept round\\\"],\n \\\"event_paths\\\":[\\\"the leader enters the accept phase at lastTriedBallot\\\",\\\"a peer with a higher bal replies with its own bal\\\",\\\"handleAcceptReply decides whether the reply counts\\\"],\n \\\"activity_classes\\\":[\\\"A1\\\"],\\\"behavior_ids\\\":[\\\"B5-slow-path-accept\\\"],\\\"fact_ids\\\":[\\\"F2-committed-decision\\\"],\n \\\"supporting_behavior_ids\\\":{\\\"B4-fast-path-decision\\\":\\\"the sibling handler where the nack branch is ordered before the ballot gate\\\",\\\"B14-ballot-monotonicity\\\":\\\"where the ballot a peer promises comes from\\\"},\n \\\"obligation_relation_kind\\\":\\\"consumption\\\",\\\"priority\\\":2,\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"scoped to the source: handleAcceptReply returns when lb.lastTriedBallot \"'!= areply.Ballot, and only after that compares the ballots again for the nack branch, so the branch is unreachable (S12-handleAcceptReply)\",\n   \"scoped to the variant run: the local construction run reports nacks 0, accept_oks 0, prepare_sent false and status unchanged after a higher-ballot reply\",\n   \"scoped to progress: the execution timeout of 10s can drive the instance into recovery independently of this handler, so the effect is a delay rather than a permanent stall (S4-execute-loop)\"],\n \"unknowns\":[\"whether the pre-accept side has any rejection signal at all, since PreAcceptReply copies the request'\"'s ballot and handlePreAccept returns silently when the request's ballot is too small\\\",\\\"whether the intended rejection path is the timeout-driven recovery in this implementation\\\"],\n \\\"trigger_rationale\\\":\\\"The accept round is part of decision formation and advancement (A1): the leader counts support and must also react to rejection, and the question asks whether the handler's own rejection branch runs at all.\\\"}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"New obligation and its first check for a dead rejection path found while reviewing the accept handler: the ballot-equality gate returns before the nack branch, so a higher-ballot AcceptReply is ignored. The harness builds the leader's accept round with the package's own constructors and delivers the reply that handleAccept sends for a peer with a higher bal; the local construction run shows nacks 0 and no reaction. The trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review decide the formal outcome, and the check is scoped to the delay this causes because the timeout-driven recovery can still advance the instance.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-accept-reply.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_accept_nack_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{},\n \\\"candidate\\\":{\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The obligation and binding are supplied with the check so the claim exists before the plan references it; the duty is the accept handler's own rejection path, bounded as a liveness cost because the timeout can advance the instance.\\\",\\\"action\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"question\\\":q,\\\"obligation\\\":claim,\\\"bindings\\\":[b8]}}\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-accept-reply.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-accept-reply.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-accept-reply.json 2>&1 | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
